[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Plainly
GenericName=Explain difficult English
Comment=Press a key and the Passage on the clipboard comes back as leveled English, glosses and a translation
Exec=plainly-desktop
Icon=dev.plainly.app
Terminal=false
Categories=Education;Utility;
# The file name and `Icon` are the identifier (`dev.plainly.app`, the one the
# config and data directories are named after), but this line is the window's
# *Wayland app_id*, and that is not the identifier: `tao` builds its
# `gtk::Application` with no application ID, so GTK publishes the program name,
# `plainly-desktop`. With Tauri's `enableGTKAppId` off — the default, and the
# one this app needs, because the built-in single-instance it turns on would take
# the launch over before `--watch`'s handover socket sees it — the app_id cannot
# be made to say `dev.plainly.app`, so the launcher has to be told what it
# actually is or it groups the window under a second, nameless icon.
StartupWMClass=plainly-desktop
Keywords=English;gloss;translation;clipboard;
